@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;desktop] mila-linux-single-instance
The application MUST use one stable GApplication id and HANDLES_OPEN activation so a second
launch forwards every `overalls://` URI to the existing process instead of creating another window.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;navigation] mila-linux-links-navigate-only
An accepted `overalls://` URI MUST select a typed navigation target only; activation MUST NOT issue a
runtime command, change a deployment, approve a session, or add credentials.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] mila-linux-route-closed-table
URI parsing MUST enforce the bounded closed route table and reject malformed authorities, unknown
paths, fragments, userinfo, encoded path segments, and non-canonical identifiers.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;architecture] mila-linux-typed-runtime-boundary
The native UI/runtime seam MUST exchange typed request and response values through a Rust trait;
raw pointers, credentials, authentication tokens, and terminal bytes MUST NOT appear in its API or
be logged by the scaffold.
